<div class="page-head"><div class="titles"><h1>Channel stock buffers</h1><p>Keep a chosen number of units out of a mapped channel’s sellable stock.</p></div></div>
<% if(locked){ %><section class="notice"><span class="badge">Growth</span> Channel buffers require Growth or above. <a class="btn" href="/settings/billing">Upgrade</a></section><% } %>
<p>Growth reviews each exact channel quantity. Pro and Custom can authorize routine buffered updates without training after the first 14 days. These controls cover governed Shopify and WooCommerce whole-unit stock mappings. They reduce oversell risk; offline channels and simultaneous external orders still need reconciliation. Amazon, eBay, POS physical counts and tracked/measured products need separate workflows.</p>
<% if(!locked&&channels.length&&locations.length){ %><section class="card section"><h2>Apply one buffer to several exact products</h2><p>Paste up to 100 SKU codes from a spreadsheet. The whole batch saves together, or none does. Products with the same buffer, channel, dispatch location and authority share one saved-rule slot.</p><form method="post" action="/autopilot/channel-buffers/batch" class="form-stack"><input type="hidden" name="_csrf" value="<%= csrfToken %>"><label class="rm-field"><span>Exact channel</span><select name="connectorId" required><option value="">Choose a mapped channel</option><% for(const c of channels){ %><option value="<%= c.id %>"><%= c.display_name %></option><% } %></select></label><label class="rm-field"><span>Exact dispatch location</span><select name="locationId" required><option value="">Choose its mapped location</option><% for(const l of locations){ %><option value="<%= l.id %>"><%= l.name %></option><% } %></select></label><label class="rm-field"><span>StockChief SKU codes, one per line</span><textarea name="skuCodes" rows="5" maxlength="20000" required></textarea></label><label class="rm-field"><span>Buffer units for each selected product</span><input type="number" name="bufferUnits" min="1" max="100000" step="1" required></label><label><input type="checkbox" name="automatic" value="yes" <%= !routineReady?'disabled':'' %>> <span class="badge">Pro / Custom</span> Apply this buffer in routine channel updates without training.</label><label><input type="checkbox" name="confirmed" value="yes" required> I confirm this exact channel, dispatch location, product list, unit buffer and authority. No physical stock changes.</label><button class="btn">Save this exact buffer batch</button></form></section><% } %>
<% if(problem){ %><p class="notice"><%= problem %></p><% } %>
<% if(selected){const p=selected.position,l=selected.local,r=selected.rule,s=selected.scope; %><section class="card section"><h2><%= s.product %> · <%= s.sku %></h2><p><%= s.provider==='shopify'?'Shopify':'WooCommerce' %> · <%= s.location %></p>
<dl class="summary-list"><div><dt>Physical stock</dt><dd><%= l.physical %> units</dd></div><div><dt>Costed stock</dt><dd><%= l.costed %> units</dd></div><div><dt>Existing commitments</dt><dd><%= l.committed %> units</dd></div><div><dt>Other reservations and holds</dt><dd><%= l.reserved %> units</dd></div><div><dt>Available before this buffer</dt><dd><%= l.unbufferedValue??l.value %> units</dd></div><div><dt>Current buffer</dt><dd><%= r?.enabled?r.buffer_units:0 %> units</dd></div><div><dt>Sellable quantity for this channel</dt><dd><strong><%= l.value %> units</strong></dd></div></dl><p>These settings change channel sellable stock. They do not receive, dispatch, write off or revalue physical inventory. Products sharing the same unit buffer, authority, channel and dispatch location use one saved-rule slot. Every product mapping is still individually checked.</p>
<form method="post" action="/autopilot/channel-buffers/<%= p.id %>/settings" class="form-stack section"><input type="hidden" name="_csrf" value="<%= csrfToken %>"><% if(r){ %><input type="hidden" name="revision" value="<%= r.revision %>"><% } %><label class="rm-field"><span>Units to keep out of this channel’s sellable stock</span><input type="number" name="bufferUnits" min="1" max="100000" step="1" required value="<%= r?.buffer_units||'' %>"></label><label><input type="checkbox" name="automatic" value="yes" <%= r?.automatic_enabled?'checked':'' %> <%= !routineReady?'disabled':'' %>> <span class="badge">Pro / Custom</span> Keep applying this exact buffer to routine stock updates, without training.</label><% if(!routineReady){ %><p>Automatic updates need Pro or Custom, the shadow period to finish and the owner’s routine authority. Saving now keeps each update under individual review.</p><% } %><label><input type="checkbox" name="confirmed" value="yes" required> I confirm this exact channel, product, dispatch location, unit buffer and level of authority.</label><button class="btn">Save this channel buffer</button></form>
<% if(r?.enabled){ %><form method="post" action="/autopilot/channel-buffer-rules/<%= r.id %>/review" class="section"><input type="hidden" name="_csrf" value="<%= csrfToken %>"><button class="btn">Prepare one exact channel update for review</button></form><% } %></section><% } %>
<% if(review&&!problem){const v=review.snapshot; %><section class="card section"><h2>Review this exact channel quantity</h2><p><%= v.profile.product %> · <%= v.profile.sku %> · <%= v.profile.location %></p><p>The channel currently reports <strong><%= v.providerValue %> sellable units</strong>. Publish <strong><%= v.value %> units</strong>, using <%= v.unbufferedValue %> currently available units minus your <%= v.bufferUnits %>-unit buffer, floored at zero.</p><p>Every send rechecks the mapping, owner, plan, authority and current stock. A changed or uncertain provider count is held for review. This review expires after 24 hours.</p><% if(delivery){ %><p><strong><%= delivery.status==='SUCCEEDED'?'Channel quantity verified':delivery.status==='AMBIGUOUS'?'Provider outcome uncertain — review the channel':delivery.status==='FAILED'?'Delivery needs review':delivery.status==='RUNNING'?'Checking channel delivery':'Queued for channel delivery' %></strong> <%= delivery.error_message||'' %></p><% } %><% if(!delivery){ %><form method="post" action="/autopilot/channel-buffer-reviews/<%= review.id %>/publish" class="form-stack"><input type="hidden" name="_csrf" value="<%= csrfToken %>"><input type="hidden" name="reviewHash" value="<%= review.reviewHash %>"><label><input type="checkbox" name="confirmed" value="yes" required> I approve publishing these exact <%= v.value %> sellable units to the channel shown above. Physical stock and accounting are unchanged.</label><button class="btn btn--primary" <%= shadow?'disabled':'' %>>Publish this exact channel quantity once</button></form><% } %></section><% } %>
<section class="card section"><h2>Mapped channel stock</h2><% if(!rows.length){ %><p>Set up a governed outbound stock mapping in <a href="/settings/connections">Connections</a>, then return here.</p><% } %><% for(const row of rows){ %><article class="section"><h3><%= row.display_name %> · <%= row.name %> · <%= row.code %></h3><p><%= row.location_name %> · <%= row.enabled?row.buffer_units+' units held back; '+(row.automatic_enabled?'routine authority configured':'individual review per update'):'No active buffer' %></p><% if(row.last_issue){ %><p class="notice"><%= row.last_issue %></p><% } %><% if(!locked){ %><a class="btn" href="/autopilot/channel-buffers?position=<%= row.id %>">Review this product buffer</a><% } %><% if(row.enabled){ %><form method="post" action="/autopilot/channel-buffers/<%= row.id %>/settings" class="form-stack section"><input type="hidden" name="_csrf" value="<%= csrfToken %>"><input type="hidden" name="revision" value="<%= row.revision %>"><label><input type="checkbox" name="confirmed" value="yes" required> Remove this buffer. Ordinary synchronization may publish more sellable units.</label><button class="btn" name="stop" value="yes">Remove buffer for future updates</button></form><% } %></article><% } %></section>
<nav aria-label="Channel stock buffer pages"><% if(page>1){ %><a href="/autopilot/channel-buffers?page=<%= page-1 %>">Previous mappings</a><% } %> <% if(more){ %><a href="/autopilot/channel-buffers?page=<%= page+1 %>">More mappings</a><% } %></nav><p>AI credits used: 0.</p>
